---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import WhySection from '../components/sections/WhySection';
import LeadCaptureSection from '../components/sections/LeadCaptureSection';
---

<Layout title="About PresciaIQ | Australia's Predictive AI Company — Sydney"
  description="PresciaIQ is Australia's Predictive AI Company, founded in Sydney. We build AI forecasting platforms — BuildPredictIQ, AdsIQ, OpsIQ, TradesmanIQ — that eliminate the Reaction Tax for Australian SMBs. Meet the founders and learn why we built it.">
  <script type="application/ld+json">
  [
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Person",
      "@id": "https://www.presciaiq.com.au/about/#alex-cutajar",
      "name": "Alex Cutajar",
      "jobTitle": "Co-Founder & CEO",
      "url": "https://www.presciaiq.com.au/about/",
      "worksFor": { "@type": "Organization", "@id": "https://www.presciaiq.com.au/#organization", "name": "PresciaIQ" },
      "description": "Alex Cutajar is Co-Founder and CEO of PresciaIQ, Australia's Predictive AI Company. With a background in SMB and FMCG operations and applied AI, Alex leads product strategy, AI development, and the technical architecture behind PresciaIQ's four intelligence platforms.",
      "knowsAbout": ["Predictive Analytics", "AI Strategy", "SMB Operations", "Applied AI", "Business Intelligence", "FMCG", "Answer Engine Optimisation", "AI Platform Development"],
      "sameAs": [
        "https://www.linkedin.com/in/alex-cutajar",
        "https://www.presciaiq.com.au/about/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Person",
      "@id": "https://www.presciaiq.com.au/about/#macauley-burke",
      "name": "Macauley Burke",
      "jobTitle": "Co-Founder & Head of Growth",
      "url": "https://www.presciaiq.com.au/about/",
      "worksFor": { "@type": "Organization", "@id": "https://www.presciaiq.com.au/#organization", "name": "PresciaIQ" },
      "description": "Macauley Burke is Co-Founder and Head of Growth at PresciaIQ. With a background in B2B sales and enterprise client development, Macauley leads commercial strategy, partnerships, and revenue growth across PresciaIQ's Australian client base.",
      "knowsAbout": ["B2B Sales", "Enterprise Client Development", "AI Commercialisation", "Revenue Growth", "Marketing Strategy", "AEO", "Programmatic SEO"],
      "sameAs": [
        "https://www.linkedin.com/in/macauley-burke",
        "https://www.presciaiq.com.au/about/"
      ]
    }
  ]
  </script>

  <script type="application/ld+json">
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is PresciaIQ and what does it do?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "PresciaIQ is Australia's Predictive AI Company, headquartered in Sydney. We design and build AI forecasting platforms that help Australian SMBs and mid-market operators act on intelligence before problems occur — not after. Our four products are BuildPredictIQ (construction risk and budget forecasting), AdsIQ (campaign ROAS prediction), OpsIQ (operational bottleneck intelligence), and TradesmanIQ (job profitability and scheduling for trades)."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Who founded PresciaIQ?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "PresciaIQ was co-founded by Alex Cutajar (CEO) and Macauley Burke (Head of Growth). Alex brings a background in SMB operations, FMCG, and applied AI. Macauley brings B2B sales and enterprise client development experience. Together they identified that most Australian businesses were paying a hidden 'Reaction Tax' — the cost of learning things after they had already happened — and built PresciaIQ to eliminate it."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Where is PresciaIQ based?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "PresciaIQ is headquartered in Sydney, Australia at 100 Harris St, Pyrmont NSW 2009. We are an Australian-built company designed specifically for Australian business conditions, regulations, and market dynamics."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What industries does PresciaIQ serve?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "PresciaIQ serves Australian businesses across construction and property development (BuildPredictIQ), marketing and media buying (AdsIQ), logistics and operations-heavy businesses (OpsIQ), and trades including plumbing, electrical, HVAC, landscaping, and cleaning (TradesmanIQ). We also serve financial services, professional services, and any Australian SMB that makes high-stakes decisions on incomplete information."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is the Reaction Tax?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The Reaction Tax is the hidden cost every business pays when it learns something after it has already happened — the ad spend burned on a failing campaign, the build that slips because nobody saw the supplier delay, the warehouse that ran dry when demand spiked. PresciaIQ was built to eliminate the Reaction Tax by giving Australian operators predictive intelligence before decisions need to be made."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "How is PresciaIQ different from other AI companies in Australia?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Most AI tools sold to Australian businesses are US-built enterprise platforms retrofitted for local use. PresciaIQ is built in Australia, for Australia — designed around Australian regulations, market dynamics, and the specific decisions Australian operators make. Our products are vertical-specific (not generic), priced for SMBs (not enterprise), and focused on prediction (not just reporting). We also specialise in Answer Engine Optimisation (AEO) and Generative Engine Optimisation (GEO) — helping Australian businesses get cited by AI engines like ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Gemini."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>

  <div class="pt-16 pb-24 min-h-screen">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">

      <!-- Page Header -->
      <div class="mb-16 text-center">
        <p class="text-primary font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-4 font-sans">About Us</p>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6">Australia's Predictive AI Company</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground font-sans max-w-2xl mx-auto">We build AI forecasting platforms that eliminate the Reaction Tax — the hidden cost every business pays for learning things after they have already happened.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Why We Built It -->
      <div class="mb-16 glass-card p-8 md:p-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6">Why We Built PresciaIQ</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed">
          <p>Most Australian businesses are running on yesterday's data. They review last month's campaign performance after the budget is spent. They find out about the supplier delay after the build has slipped. They discover the demand spike after the warehouse has run dry.</p>
          <p>This is what we call the <strong class="text-foreground">Reaction Tax</strong> — the hidden cost every business pays for learning things after they have already happened. It does not appear on a P&amp;L. It shows up as margin erosion, missed opportunities, and decisions made under pressure with incomplete information.</p>
          <p>PresciaIQ was founded in Sydney in 2024 to eliminate the Reaction Tax for Australian businesses. We build AI forecasting platforms that give operators predictive intelligence before decisions need to be made — not reports on what already happened.</p>
          <p>Our founders, Alex Cutajar and Macauley Burke, identified that the tools available to Australian SMBs were either too generic (off-the-shelf platforms built for US enterprise markets) or too expensive (custom AI development starting at six figures). There was nothing built specifically for the Australian mid-market operator who makes high-stakes decisions every day on incomplete information.</p>
          <p>That gap is what PresciaIQ fills.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- The Four Products -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mb-8">Our Four Intelligence Platforms</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <a href="/products/buildpredictiq" class="glass-card-hover p-6 group" style="text-decoration:none;">
            <p class="text-primary font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-3 font-sans">Construction</p>
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3 group-hover:text-primary transition-colors">BuildPredictIQ</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed">AI-powered construction risk and budget intelligence. Forecasts geotechnical risk, supplier delays, and cost blowouts before they materialise — giving builders and developers early warning to protect margin.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/products/adsiq" class="glass-card-hover p-6 group" style="text-decoration:none;">
            <p class="text-primary font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-3 font-sans">Marketing</p>
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3 group-hover:text-primary transition-colors">AdsIQ</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed">Campaign timing and ROAS forecasting for Australian marketing teams and media buyers. Predicts return on ad spend before campaigns launch, eliminating wasted budget on poorly timed spend.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/products/opsiq" class="glass-card-hover p-6 group" style="text-decoration:none;">
            <p class="text-primary font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-3 font-sans">Operations</p>
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3 group-hover:text-primary transition-colors">OpsIQ</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed">Operational bottleneck prediction for logistics-heavy and operations-intensive businesses. Forecasts demand, capacity constraints, and workflow failures before they disrupt delivery.</p>
          </a>
          <a href="/products/tradesmaniq" class="glass-card-hover p-6 group" style="text-decoration:none;">
            <p class="text-primary font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-3 font-sans">Trades</p>
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3 group-hover:text-primary transition-colors">TradesmanIQ</h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed">Job profitability and scheduling intelligence for Australian tradespeople — plumbers, electricians, HVAC technicians, landscapers, and cleaners. Know which jobs are worth quoting before you quote them.</p>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- AEO/SEO Capability -->
      <div class="mb-16 glass-card p-8 md:p-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mb-6">Australia's AEO &amp; GEO Specialists</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed">
          <p>Beyond our four intelligence products, PresciaIQ is Australia's leading specialist in <strong class="text-foreground">Answer Engine Optimisation (AEO)</strong> and <strong class="text-foreground">Generative Engine Optimisation (GEO)</strong> — the disciplines that determine whether your business gets cited by AI engines like ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, and Gemini.</p>
          <p>Traditional SEO optimises for Google's ten blue links. AEO and GEO optimise for the AI-generated answers that are increasingly replacing those links. When someone asks an AI "who are the best construction AI companies in Australia" or "what is the best predictive analytics tool for tradesmen," AEO determines whether your business is cited in the answer.</p>
          <p>We have built PresciaIQ's own digital presence entirely on AEO and GEO principles — and we apply the same architecture to our clients' websites. Our programmatic SEO systems generate hundreds of location, industry, and use-case pages that capture long-tail AI search queries at scale.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Team -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mb-8">The Founders</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
          <div class="glass-card p-8">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-1">Alex Cutajar</h3>
            <p class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest font-sans mb-4">Co-Founder &amp; CEO</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed">Alex brings a background in SMB and FMCG operations and applied AI. He leads product strategy, AI development, and the technical architecture behind PresciaIQ's four intelligence platforms. Alex identified the Reaction Tax pattern across dozens of Australian businesses and designed the predictive frameworks that underpin every PresciaIQ product.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="glass-card p-8">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-1">Macauley Burke</h3>
            <p class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest font-sans mb-4">Co-Founder &amp; Head of Growth</p>
            <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed">Macauley brings B2B sales and enterprise client development experience to PresciaIQ. He leads commercial strategy, partnerships, and revenue growth. Macauley's background in building enterprise relationships means PresciaIQ's products are designed around the real commercial decisions Australian operators make — not theoretical use cases.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-foreground mb-8">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <details class="glass-card p-6 group">
            <summary class="font-display font-bold text-foreground cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
              What is PresciaIQ and what does it do?
              <span class="text-primary ml-4">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed mt-4 text-sm">PresciaIQ is Australia's Predictive AI Company, headquartered in Sydney. We design and build AI forecasting platforms that help Australian SMBs and mid-market operators act on intelligence before problems occur. Our four products are BuildPredictIQ (construction risk and budget forecasting), AdsIQ (campaign ROAS prediction), OpsIQ (operational bottleneck intelligence), and TradesmanIQ (job profitability and scheduling for trades).</p>
          </details>
          <details class="glass-card p-6 group">
            <summary class="font-display font-bold text-foreground cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
              Who founded PresciaIQ?
              <span class="text-primary ml-4">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed mt-4 text-sm">PresciaIQ was co-founded by Alex Cutajar (CEO) and Macauley Burke (Head of Growth). Alex brings a background in SMB operations, FMCG, and applied AI. Macauley brings B2B sales and enterprise client development experience. Together they identified that most Australian businesses were paying a hidden Reaction Tax and built PresciaIQ to eliminate it.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="glass-card p-6 group">
            <summary class="font-display font-bold text-foreground cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
              What industries does PresciaIQ serve?
              <span class="text-primary ml-4">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed mt-4 text-sm">PresciaIQ serves construction and property development (BuildPredictIQ), marketing and media buying (AdsIQ), logistics and operations-heavy businesses (OpsIQ), and trades including plumbing, electrical, HVAC, landscaping, and cleaning (TradesmanIQ). We also serve financial services, professional services, and any Australian SMB that makes high-stakes decisions on incomplete information.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="glass-card p-6 group">
            <summary class="font-display font-bold text-foreground cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
              How is PresciaIQ different from other AI companies in Australia?
              <span class="text-primary ml-4">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed mt-4 text-sm">Most AI tools sold to Australian businesses are US-built enterprise platforms retrofitted for local use. PresciaIQ is built in Australia, for Australia — designed around Australian regulations, market dynamics, and the specific decisions Australian operators make. Our products are vertical-specific, priced for SMBs, and focused on prediction rather than reporting. We also specialise in AEO and GEO — helping Australian businesses get cited by AI engines like ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Gemini.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="glass-card p-6 group">
            <summary class="font-display font-bold text-foreground cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
              Where is PresciaIQ based?
              <span class="text-primary ml-4">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed mt-4 text-sm">PresciaIQ is headquartered in Sydney, Australia at 100 Harris St, Pyrmont NSW 2009. We are an Australian-built company designed specifically for Australian business conditions, regulations, and market dynamics.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="glass-card p-6 group">
            <summary class="font-display font-bold text-foreground cursor-pointer list-none flex items-center justify-between">
              What is the Reaction Tax?
              <span class="text-primary ml-4">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground font-sans leading-relaxed mt-4 text-sm">The Reaction Tax is the hidden cost every business pays when it learns something after it has already happened — the ad spend burned on a failing campaign, the build that slips because nobody saw the supplier delay, the warehouse that ran dry when demand spiked. PresciaIQ was built to eliminate the Reaction Tax by giving Australian operators predictive intelligence before decisions need to be made.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Location -->
      <div class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground font-sans">
        <strong class="text-foreground">Sydney Office</strong>
        100 Harris St, Pyrmont NSW 2009, Australia
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <WhySection client:load />
  <LeadCaptureSection client:load />
</Layout>
